            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardial infarction associated with myocardial bridging: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>537-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of a 41-year-old woman with chest pain for 1 hour who was admitted to our emergency room with acute myocardial infarction. Coronary angiography and spiral computer tomography showed myocardial bridging and an intracoronary thrombus in the mid-segment of the left anterior descending artery. She felt better after taking aspirin, diltiazem and a beta blocker and was discharged 15 days later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
